{
  "_notes": [
    "Breakshot 1.3 (1996, Capcom).",
    "Capcom 16-bit bus: 8-bit NVRAM data on D0-D7, actual data at even file positions.",
    "CPU address = 0x30000000 + even_index * 2.",
    "Scores stored as score/10 (scale: 10). Verified against NVRAM data with real scores.",
    "Includes Cutthroat Champions table."
  ],
  "_fileformat": 0.8,
  "_metadata": {
    "version": 5,
    "copyright": [
      "Copyright (C) 2026 by Tom Collins <tom@scorbit.io>",
      "Copyright (C) 2026 by Andre Santana <herrmirto@proton.me>"
    ],
    "license": "GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0",
    "platform": "capcom",
    "roms": [
      "bsv103"
    ]
  },
  "game_state": {
    "final_scores_order": "most_recent_first",
    "final_scores": [
      {
        "label": "Recent Game 1 (newest)",
        "encoding": "int",
        "endian": "big",
        "scale": 10,
        "offsets": [
          "0x30001EEA",
          "0x30001EEC",
          "0x30001EEE",
          "0x30001EF0"
        ],
        "_notes": [
          "Recent-games buffer in battery DRAM (.nv file offset 0x1EEA), newest completed entry first; one push per player at game over, last player first. Verified with a real 4-player game (P1 765,350 / P2 396,250 / P3 272,400 / P4 168,090 read back as entries 4..1 exactly), on top of three older real games (3,114,990 / 3,292,410 / 858,390). Same structure as Big Bang Bar but at a title-specific base (bbb109 uses 0x205E). Breakshot has no usable player_count byte anywhere in DRAM (full 512KB triangulated); the plugin infers the player count from the number of entries pushed on top of the session-start baseline."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Recent Game 2",
        "encoding": "int",
        "endian": "big",
        "scale": 10,
        "offsets": [
          "0x30001EF2",
          "0x30001EF4",
          "0x30001EF6",
          "0x30001EF8"
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Recent Game 3",
        "encoding": "int",
        "endian": "big",
        "scale": 10,
        "offsets": [
          "0x30001EFA",
          "0x30001EFC",
          "0x30001EFE",
          "0x30001F00"
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Recent Game 4 (oldest)",
        "encoding": "int",
        "endian": "big",
        "scale": 10,
        "offsets": [
          "0x30001F02",
          "0x30001F04",
          "0x30001F06",
          "0x30001F08"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "credits": {
      "label": "Credits",
      "start": "0x30000010",
      "encoding": "int",
      "length": 1,
      "_notes": [
        "Battery DRAM, platform-wide: verified against user-reported credit counts on bbb109 (7), bsv103 (5) and pmv112 (4), and observed incrementing on coin insertion in a headless probe. (0x3000139C, previously mapped, is a different counter that only coincidentally matched on bbb/bsv.)"
      ]
    },
    "game_over": {
      "_notes": [
        "Game-in-progress flag in DRAM (volatile RAM, not in the .nv). Found via libpinmame, verified across Breakshot/Big Bang Bar/Pinball Magic: 0x000012F2 bit 0x40 is SET during a game, CLEAR in attract and at game over. invert=true so the field reads true when the game is over."
      ],
      "label": "Game Over",
      "start": "0x000012F2",
      "encoding": "bool",
      "mask": "0x40",
      "invert": true
    },
    "_notes": [
      "scores was removed: all four player entries aliased the NVRAM high-score mirror at 0x300000F0, so they reported leaderboard values instead of the game being played. Capcom keeps live scores in volatile DRAM (verified for bbb109 Player 1 at 0x00061F32); each game needs its own verified address before scores can be reinstated."
    ]
  },
